/P 80 0 R
/T (A drone must stay balanced against wind, follow commands, and often perform tasks such as mapping or obstacle avoidance, while carrying its own battery. Its computer system must therefore be light, compact and economical in power, which is a difficult design problem. The main problem can be stated as: How can the computer organization of a drone provide fast and deterministic real-time control, reliable sensor and communication interfaces, and enough processing capability for advanced tasks such as navigation and vision, while keeping weight, power consumption, cost and heat to a minimum, and while remaining safe in the presence of faults?)
/E (A drone must stay balanced against wind, follow commands, and often perform tasks such as mapping or obstacle avoidance, while carrying its own battery. Its computer system must therefore be light, compact and economical in power, which is a difficult design problem. The main problem can be stated as: How can the computer organization of a drone provide fast and deterministic real-time control, reliable sensor and communication interfaces, and enough processing capability for advanced tasks such as navigation and vision, while keeping weight, power consumption, cost and heat to a minimum, and while remaining safe in the presence of faults?)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
