/T (The organization of a typical quadcopter is shown in Figure 2. The flight controller is at the centre. Sensors feed data into it, the radio link brings commands from the pilot or ground station, and its outputs go to the four ESCs that drive the motors. A battery and power distribution board supply energy to all units, and a storage device records flight data. A companion computer, when present, communicates with the flight controller over a serial link.)
/E (The organization of a typical quadcopter is shown in Figure 2. The flight controller is at the centre. Sensors feed data into it, the radio link brings commands from the pilot or ground station, and its outputs go to the four ESCs that drive the motors. A battery and power distribution board supply energy to all units, and a storage device records flight data. A companion computer, when present, communicates with the flight controller over a serial link.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
