/T (The CPU of the flight controller is normally a 32-bit ARM Cortex-M core. Like any CPU, it has a control unit that fetches and decodes instructions, an ALU that carries out arithmetic and logical operations, and a set of registers that hold operands, addresses and the program counter. The instruction cycle of fetch, decode, execute and store is repeated)
/E (The CPU of the flight controller is normally a 32-bit ARM Cortex-M core. Like any CPU, it has a control unit that fetches and decodes instructions, an ALU that carries out arithmetic and logical operations, and a set of registers that hold operands, addresses and the program counter. The instruction cycle of fetch, decode, execute and store is repeated)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
