/P 83 0 R
/T (Every function of the flight controller is based on digital logic. The ALU is built from adders, comparators, shifters and logic gates. Registers and memory cells are made from flip-flops and latches. Multiplexers select among multiple data sources, decoders select a memory location or peripheral from an address, and counters form the heart of timers. Analog-to-digital conversion. Battery voltage, current and some sensors give analog outputs. An ADC samples the signal and converts it to a binary number. For an n-bit)
/E (Every function of the flight controller is based on digital logic. The ALU is built from adders, comparators, shifters and logic gates. Registers and memory cells are made from flip-flops and latches. Multiplexers select among multiple data sources, decoders select a memory location or peripheral from an address, and counters form the heart of timers. Analog-to-digital conversion. Battery voltage, current and some sensors give analog outputs. An ADC samples the signal and converts it to a binary number. For an n-bit)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
