/T (The state estimation commonly uses a complementary filter or an Extended Kalman Filter \(EKF\). Both are matrix-and-vector calculations that make heavy use of the multiplier and floating-point unit. The gyroscope gives accurate short-term angular rate but drifts over time, whereas the accelerometer gives a long-term gravity reference but is noisy during manoeuvres; combining the two gives a stable and accurate attitude estimate.)
/E (The state estimation commonly uses a complementary filter or an Extended Kalman Filter \(EKF\). Both are matrix-and-vector calculations that make heavy use of the multiplier and floating-point unit. The gyroscope gives accurate short-term angular rate but drifts over time, whereas the accelerometer gives a long-term gravity reference but is noisy during manoeuvres; combining the two gives a stable and accurate attitude estimate.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [12]
>>
