320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 85 0 R
/T (7. Companion Computer and Specialized Processing)
/E (7. Companion Computer and Specialized Processing)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 85 0 R
/T (When a drone must interpret camera images, build a map or avoid obstacles, the processing requirement is far above what a microcontroller can supply. The drone therefore adds a companion computer, which is normally a multi-core ARM processor with a GPU and sometimes a neural processing unit \(NPU\). It runs a full operating system such as Linux and communicates with the flight controller through a UART or Ethernet link, using a lightweight message protocol. The companion computer sends high-level commands such as velocity or waypoint setpoints, but the flight controller always keeps the final responsibility for stability.)
/E (When a drone must interpret camera images, build a map or avoid obstacles, the processing requirement is far above what a microcontroller can supply. The drone therefore adds a companion computer, which is normally a multi-core ARM processor with a GPU and sometimes a neural processing unit \(NPU\). It runs a full operating system such as Linux and communicates with the flight controller through a UART or Ethernet link, using a lightweight message protocol. The companion computer sends high-level commands such as velocity or waypoint setpoints, but the flight controller always keeps the final responsibility for stability.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 85 0 R
/T (This arrangement shows the same principle seen in smartphone SoCs: specialized hardware, such as a GPU or NPU, can execute a certain class of workload far more efficiently than a general-purpose CPU. It also isolates the safety-critical control loop from non-deterministic software. If the companion computer crashes, the flight controller can still hold the aircraft stable or return to land.)
/E (This arrangement shows the same principle seen in smartphone SoCs: specialized hardware, such as a GPU or NPU, can execute a certain class of workload far more efficiently than a general-purpose CPU. It also isolates the safety-critical control loop from non-deterministic software. If the companion computer crashes, the flight controller can still hold the aircraft stable or return to land.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 85 0 R
/T (8. Power Management)
/E (8. Power Management)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (11)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
325 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (3.3 V rails for the processor and sensors. Power modules measure the battery voltage and current, which are read by the ADC to estimate remaining capacity and trigger a low-battery failsafe. Clean power is essential, because switching noise from motors can disturb sensors and cause incorrect readings, so filtering capacitors and separate regulators are used.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 86 0 R
/T (9. Reliability and Fault Tolerance)
/E (9. Reliability and Fault Tolerance)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Because a computer fault in flight can cause damage or injury, drones include several protective mechanisms in their organization:)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
328 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E <80>
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Watchdog timer: A hardware counter that resets the processor if the software fails to refresh it within a set time, recovering from a software hang.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Sensor redundancy: Larger drones carry multiple IMUs, compasses and GPS units, and the software switches to a healthy one when another fails.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Failsafe logic: Loss of the radio link, low battery or a geofence breach triggers a programmed response such as hovering, landing or returning to the launch point. Error detection: Checksums and CRCs on telemetry and storage data detect corrupted data, and parity or ECC may protect memory in higher-grade controllers. Pre-arm checks: The software verifies sensors, calibration, battery and communications before it allows the motors to start.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
