338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The analysis of the computer organization of drones leads to the following findings.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 87 0 R
/T (Finding 1: A drone is a complete embedded computer system)
/E (Finding 1: A drone is a complete embedded computer system)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (A drone contains every unit of a computer: a CPU, memory, input devices, output devices, buses and a clock. The only difference from a desktop computer is that all these units are small, specialized and permanently dedicated to one task, flight control.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 87 0 R
/T (Finding 2: Real-time performance matters more than raw speed)
/E (Finding 2: Real-time performance matters more than raw speed)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The success of the system depends on meeting deadlines in every control cycle. Predictable timing, achieved through hardware timers, interrupts, DMA and prioritised tasks, is more valuable than a high clock rate.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 87 0 R
/T (Finding 3: Digital building blocks are directly visible)
/E (Finding 3: Digital building blocks are directly visible)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (Counters, comparators, registers, multiplexers, decoders, adders and ADCs appear in the processor, timer and sensor interfaces of the drone. This shows how the theory of digital principles is applied in real devices.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 87 0 R
/T (Finding 4: Dedicated hardware reduces the CPU burden)
/E (Finding 4: Dedicated hardware reduces the CPU burden)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (Timers generate PWM signals, DMA moves data, the FPU performs fractional calculations, and the ESC commutates the motors. Each of these offloads work from the CPU and makes the total system more efficient and deterministic.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 87 0 R
/T (Finding 5: Sensor fusion turns noisy data into reliable information)
/E (Finding 5: Sensor fusion turns noisy data into reliable information)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (No single sensor is good enough alone. Combining gyroscope, accelerometer, magnetometer, barometer and GPS data with filters gives an accurate estimate of the state of the aircraft, and this needs significant arithmetic capability.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 87 0 R
/T (Finding 6: Two-level processing improves safety and capability)
/E (Finding 6: Two-level processing improves safety and capability)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (Separating the flight controller from the companion computer allows intelligent features without risking the stability of flight. Each processor is matched to its own kind of workload.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 87 0 R
/T (Finding 7: Fault tolerance is part of the organization)
/E (Finding 7: Fault tolerance is part of the organization)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (Watchdog timers, redundant sensors, failsafe logic and error detection are built into the system, so that failures lead to a safe outcome rather than a crash.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
