/P 88 0 R
/E (Based on the analysis and the findings, the following recommendations can be considered for an efficient and reliable drone computer system.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 88 0 R
/T (Use processors with hardware floating-point and DSP support)
/E (Use processors with hardware floating-point and DSP support)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (Control and sensor-fusion algorithms are calculation-intensive. A microcontroller with an FPU and multiply-accumulate instructions completes them quickly and with a good margin for deadlines.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 88 0 R
/T (Use a real-time operating system with clear task priorities)
/E (Use a real-time operating system with clear task priorities)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (The fastest control loop should have the highest priority, and logging, telemetry and navigation should run at lower priority so that they never delay flight stabilisation.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 88 0 R
/T (Use dedicated hardware timers for motor outputs)
/E (Use dedicated hardware timers for motor outputs)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (Generating PWM or digital motor signals in hardware avoids software jitter and gives precise motor control.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
362 0 obj
<<
