/Title (The history of unmanned aircraft goes back to the early twentieth century, when simple radio-controlled aircraft were built mainly as military target vehicles. Their control systems were analog: relays, vacuum tubes and, later, discrete transistor circuits. The pilot's commands were converted directly into movement of the control surfaces, and there was no onboard computation of any significant kind.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 669 0 R
/Next 830 0 R
>>
endobj
774 0 obj
<<
/Title (A second important background idea is that of the embedded system. A drone computer has a fixed purpose and is permanently built into the machine it controls. It has no keyboard or monitor and typically no conventional operating system. Its software is designed around the hardware, and its performance is judged by determinism and reliability rather than by raw speed.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 669 0 R
/Prev 831 0 R
>>
endobj
