902 0 obj
<<
/Title (Different data-transfer techniques are used according to the need. Programmed I/O is used for slow devices and configuration. Interrupt-driven I/O is used for events such as data-ready signals. Direct Memory Access \(DMA\) is used for fast, continuous transfers, for example reading IMU samples or receiving serial data. With DMA the data move between a peripheral and memory without CPU involvement, so the CPU remains free for the control computation.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 882 0 R
/Prev 901 0 R
>>
endobj
